CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts
^\[foo\.loop_assigns\.\d+\] line 8 Check assigns clause inclusion for loop .*: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
The condition of a conditional target in a loop assigns clause may call a
side-effect-free function. DFCC inlines that call, without a write set
argument, when it generates the loop write set. Instrumenting cond, which is
neither reachable from the entry point nor called from a function contract,
made goto-instrument fail with "not enough arguments when inlining goto
program".
